Adds support for explicit asm("reg") / __asm__("reg") register parameter
constraints in function declarations for the m68k-amiga-elf toolchain.

Enables vbcc/SAS-C-style AmigaOS register parameter syntax:

  /* Both asm() and __asm__() are accepted */
  void DevOpen(struct ExecBase  *SysBase asm("a6"),
               struct IORequest *ioreq   asm("a1"),
               ULONG             unit    asm("d0"),
               ULONG             flags   asm("d1"));

Register parameters are supported on function *definitions*: the callee
receives each annotated argument in the named register, and C callers in
the same translation unit load the registers at the call site (no stack
slot in either direction).  Annotated prototypes, typedefs and function
pointers are rejected with a hard error, since a caller seeing only a
prototype would otherwise silently use the stack ABI while the definition
reads registers.  Sibcalls to register-parameter functions are disabled
because the sibcall epilogue would clobber arguments living in call-saved
registers (d2-d7/a2-a5).

Changes:
  gcc/config/m68k/m68k.h   - FUNCTION_ARG_REGNO_P, CUMULATIVE_ARGS struct
                              (+fndecl), INIT_CUMULATIVE_INCOMING_ARGS
  gcc/config/m68k/m68k.cc  - m68k_get_parm_regno, m68k_function_arg,
                              m68k_function_arg_advance, sibcall guard
  gcc/c/c-tree.h            - asm_name field in struct c_parm, build_c_parm
  gcc/c/c-decl.cc           - build_c_parm, grokparm, push_parm_decl,
                              grokparms (prototype rejection),
                              store_parm_decls (register map attribute)
  gcc/c/c-parser.cc         - parse asm() after parameter declarator

Apply after gcc-barto.patch:
  patch -p1 < gcc-barto.patch
  patch -p1 < gcc-regparm.patch

